{#
    One member's share: how many subscriptions it is.

    The members screen draws a row per member and the dashboard draws a card
    of them, but what a share's count *is* — subscriptions carried, with the
    one-off entries kept out of the money beside it — is one thing, so it is
    written once. Two copies would eventually be two answers.

    The money itself is not here. Both callers take it from
    `dashboard/_headline.twig`, which applies the per-currency rule rather than
    restating it.
#}

{#
    The count, and the one-off entries kept out of the money beside it.

    They are counted and not costed on purpose: a lifetime licence spread over
    a month is a number that means nothing, and the tiles above the dashboard
    already keep the two apart for exactly the same reason.
#}
{% macro count(row) %}
    {{ t('household.subscriptions_count', { 'count': row.subscription_count }) }}
    {%- if row.one_off_count %}
        <span class="hint">{{ t('household.one_off_count', { 'count': row.one_off_count }) }}</span>
    {%- endif %}
{% endmacro %}
